#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5178
msgid "Sort Order"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5180
msgid ""
"Description: Whether to sort file and folder names case-sensitively in the "
"project panel. This setting works in combination with `sort_mode`. "
"`sort_mode` controls how files and directories are grouped (e.g., "
"directories first), while this setting controls how names are compared "
"within those groups."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5181
msgid "Setting: `sort_order`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5182
msgid "Default: `default`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5186
msgid ""
"Case-insensitive natural sort with lowercase preferred in ties. Numbers in "
"file names are compared by their numeric value (e.g., `file2` sorts before "
"`file10`). Names that differ only in casing are sorted with lowercase first "
"(e.g., `apple` before `Apple`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5191 src/reference/all-settings.md:5201
#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5211 src/reference/all-settings.md:5221
msgid "\"sort_order\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5196
msgid ""
"Uppercase names are grouped before lowercase names, with case-insensitive "
"natural sort within each group. Dot-prefixed names (e.g., `.gitignore`) sort "
"before both groups. Accented uppercase letters like `É` are treated as "
"uppercase."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5201
msgid "\"upper\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5206
msgid ""
"Lowercase names are grouped before uppercase names, with case-insensitive "
"natural sort within each group. Dot-prefixed names sort before both groups."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5211
msgid "\"lower\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5216
msgid ""
"Pure Unicode codepoint comparison. No case folding and no natural number "
"sorting. Uppercase ASCII letters (`A`–`Z`) sort before lowercase (`a`–`z`) "
"as a natural consequence of their codepoint values. Accented characters like "
"`É` (U+00C9) sort after all ASCII letters. Numbers are compared "
"lexicographically (`file10` sorts before `file2`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/all-settings.md:5221
msgid "\"unicode\""
msgstr ""

